            "review_title": "Review at Lotus Blanc Cafe Restaurant",
            "review_text": "N0bleGuy\nLondon, United Kingdom151 contributions\n0\nLoved it Here - Poor Reviews a Little Unfair...\nMar 2019 • Friends\nWe've been in Hanoi for 4 days and we've been repeatedly ripped off by taxi drivers pretending the 500,000 I just gave him was a 20,000, the same till girl at Highlands Coffee trying to short-change us on each of our 3 visits, and our hotel selling our rooms for the night we're still due to be there, and offering no discount to 'help' them and vacate early!\n\nYet, in all this, we went to this restaurant on our first night and the server there was brilliant. She spoke good English and I think she picked up that we were annoyed by the taxi scam, so she engaged us (admittedly at the expense of other guests, really sorry we didn't mean to take all her attention...), she supplied us with information about Ho Chi Min's mausoleum and was generally lovely.\n\nThe food we had was decent as well, the beer was reasonably priced and at the very end our waitress actually tried to refuse the tip we gave her because we'd been ripped off by the taxi driver earlier. How many servers do you know that would turn down a tip from a Westerner when they're really not earning a great amount?\n\nWe were inside but there's a small balcony with three or four tables allowing you to watch the world go by.\n\nI'd give it a try - they're honest and deserve a chance :)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 16, 2019",
